aming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T12:05:39-07:00","id":295058,"title":"","content":"Werewolf: The Forsaken - You're basically in a cult-clan, and your magical powers are barely enough to keep you alive in the face of overwhelming opposition. Life sucks.<br /> <br /> Vampire: The Requiem - You're basically in the mob, and your magical powers won't stop you from burning in sunlight. Unlife sucks.<br /> <br /> Promethean: the Created - You're basically a pariah, and your magical powers don't really help you get out of being shunned by everything. Proto-life sucks.<br /> <br /> Changeling: The Lost - Your identity and part of your soul was stolen by The Man who is now out to get you, and your magical powers won't help. Half-life sucks. <br /> <br /> Geist: The Sin Eaters - You hear voices and ghosts pester you, but you're super-resilient now and have some other neat magical powers. Second life is pretty good.<br /> <br /> Mummy: The Curse - You're worshipped as a god, and you've got magical powers to match... for a day or two, and then you degrade into a feeble old person. Returned-life is a mixed bag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tum